#  as_tv wpctl set-volume @DEFAULT_AUDIO_SINK@ 30% && as_tv wpctl set-mute @DEFAULT_AUDIO_SINK@ 0; } &


# ---- Connect a Bluetooth keyboard by its address (needs a USB Bluetooth dongle) -------------
# The first time, put the keyboard in pairing mode before Debian boots (or before
# "sudo systemctl restart netcast-rclocal"): this finds it and pairs it. The pairing is kept
# in debian.img, so after that it only connects it, retrying for 2 minutes in case the
# keyboard is still asleep. If the keyboard asks for a code, pair it once from the Bluetooth
# icon in the panel instead. Find the address with "bluetoothctl devices" (once paired) or
# "bluetoothctl --timeout 20 scan on" (in pairing mode).
